From 8f423e7ba6119f8828a5b4bf5aa0025331d772cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:38:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Restore WineForge copyright and provenance notices

Code ported from WineForge (Radim Vesely) had its notices rebranded on
the way in: "Copyright (C) 2026 Radim Vesely for WineForge" became
"... for MetalSharp", WineForge-Internal/WineForge-Feature provenance
markers and "WineForge launcher-compat" comments became MetalSharp ones,
and the WFUSync headers described the code as MetalSharp's.

Restore the original copyright lines, provenance markers and file
descriptions in every affected file. Where MetalSharp Wine modified the
code (msync is WineForge's WFUSync renamed; WFDXCompat runs on Mullion
instead of D3DMetal), say so next to the original notice instead of in
place of it. The LGPL notices were already intact.
